{"name":"Ice Dream","hex":"#eaebe1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2/B language code for Icelandic."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water in frozen (solid) form.","Any frozen volatile chemical, such as ammonia or carbon dioxide."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ice"},{"term":"dream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Imaginary events seen in the mind while sleeping.","A hope or wish."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To see imaginary events in one's mind while sleeping.","To hope, to wish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg/330px-Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice","wikidata":"Q23392"},{"title":"Dream","blocks":[{"text":"A dream is a succession of images, dynamic scenes and situations, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep. Humans generally spend more than two hours dreaming per night, and each dream lasts around 5–20 minutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg/330px-A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg?utm_sourc